{"type":"text","timestamp":1790891383626,"sessionID":"ses_f068ebceaffeiHeFWknD61RRtp","part":{"id":"prt_0f971c81b001WnyrbuDjm4ZW06","messageID":"msg_0f971c0ec001365eeT4Qi4se5b","sessionID":"ses_f068ebceaffeiHeFWknD61RRtp","type":"text","text":"Submitted. Summary of findings from `src/cachetools/__init__.py` (`TTLCache`, standard implementation, monotonic timer by default):\n\n- **visible_at_deadline: false** — `__contains__` returns `self.timer() < link.expires`, a strict less-than, so at the exact expiration time the entry is no longer visible via membership.\n- **expired_read_removes_storage: false** — an expired `__getitem__` calls `self.__missing__(key)`, which in the base `Cache` just `raise KeyError(key)`; the underlying stored value is not physically deleted (only `expire()`/`__delitem__` do that).\n- **assignment_refreshes_deadline: true** — `__setitem__` reuses the existing link (`link.unlink()`) and always sets `link.expires = time + self.__ttl`, refreshing the deadline for live entries.\n- **expire_reports_removed_pairs: true** — `expire()` builds `expired.append((curr.key, cache_getitem(self, curr.key)))` while deleting each entry and `return expired`, so it reports the removed `(key, value)` pairs.","time":{"start":1790891378715,"end":1790891383619}}}
